{"title":"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 29","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Linear_Algebra)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Linear Algebra)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>You plot weight <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/0/c1044113dca0096541d8e9fb5a8f6c24b8dc09dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"18\" /> against height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b558769a96459d2be8d1b67f24da056bb02f6399.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"23\" height=\"18\" /> for three of your friends and obtain the points \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/8/b881908c1a890e3a16ae967f9303a851ba5d96e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_{1},y_{1}), (x_{2},y_{2}), (x_{3},y_{3})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"184\" height=\"18\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f3767b0241651e7f77e4006364c7dde96871645d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{1} &lt; x_{2} &lt; x_{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"100\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/8/488ce7ed47d1d7957ab11e7777b1d7047e4811d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{3} - x_{2} = x_{2} - x_{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"138\" height=\"10\" />, \nwhich of the following is necessarily the slope of the line which best fits the data? \n\"Best fits\" means that the sum of the squares of the vertical distances from the data points to the line is smaller than for any other line.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/e/6be31f3ecf7ba232c0322b6d88d802b03cb6524d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{y_{3}-y_{1}}{x_{3}-x_{1}}\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{(y_{2}-y_{1})-(y_{3}-y_{2})}{x_{3}-x_{1}}\\qquad\\\\ \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{2y_{3}-y_{1}-y_{2}}{2x_{3}-x_{1}-x_{2}}\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{y_{2}-y_{1}}{x_{2}-x_{1}}+\\frac{y_{3}-y_{2}}{x_{3}-x_{2}}\\qquad\\\\ \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{none of these}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"357\" height=\"100\" /> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/6/536a3bcee68d746371a8631e091ea01c6dc19835.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = mx + b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"90\" height=\"16\" /> a prediction line, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/2/0c2685354f112460fc6f21ec71e027db081d04a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = x_3 - x_2 = x_2 - x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"176\" height=\"17\" />.  Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/d/bad7c2113d8a36242a2b6fb2b2a1f9e54d6e32a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 = x_2 - d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/d/97dc330608028986862dfa68872a3cd3f12a10aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_3 = x_2 + d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"17\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/5/5f56dd57e43d802e24ea798546bbd4f7530361d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_1 = mx_1 + b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/9/769673cf0f57fbacfd4099079131a3e908d03981.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_2 = mx_2 + b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/b/02bd64c90d1bcb1022ec774242b0145f04ef9434.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_3 = mx_3 + b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"17\" /> be the predicted values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/e/4ae250d1bdd46e5677f27edcf5efb34587b6fc1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"14\" height=\"11\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/2/0320ab2ddd4939f9072e5316fe8888b0cddee319.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"11\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/8/9489ac80de3e095e70ff6749cd030067dd3a398f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"11\" />, respectively.  Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/f/bafea92926eb79ad1aa74f9619e52cf7f257b4c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_1 = m(x_2 - d) + b = z_2 - md$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"239\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/b/c0bbb709131c067ef401f316e875cf0ce794988b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_3 = m(x_2 + d) + b = z_2 + md$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"239\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Consider all lines that pass through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/e/40ea4275d540816092246deb396dcee26f1a1a95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_2, z_2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"58\" height=\"20\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/2/d8224c429895524438447c747d23040c33d064d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1 = z_1 - y_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/3/513ad490268252e0a543b17a220d5d38e9a68adf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_2 = z_2 - y_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/8/268489cf10993998b9813a14ecea3e9b526073df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_3 = z_3 - y_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"16\" /> be the three residuals.  Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/6/cd6cd9d34938f1b5b74ae3f7b472cb55265e2f20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1 + r_3 = z_1 + z_3 - y_1 - y_3 = z_2 + md + z_2 - md - y_1 - y_3 = 2z_2 - y_1 - y_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"588\" height=\"18\" />.  So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/9/a99c1952dc0a56577b80e4509dd0b3766c576d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1 + r_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" /> is the same for all these lines, as is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b4f3f4b698ce35667432041e168f7653533fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/f/befd7e9b4a79e7e171971d3b3c7d3ed8f5bbce78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s = r_1 + r_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"15\" />.  \n</p><p>Since the best line passing through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/e/40ea4275d540816092246deb396dcee26f1a1a95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_2, z_2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"58\" height=\"20\" /> must minimize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/4/23416440840fc591155e0dd236d4c066d7d1e81c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1^2 + r_2^2 + r_3^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"95\" height=\"21\" />, it must minimize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/f/54f7464eb723e154643dba713e7b86d267fc2a3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1^2 + r_3^2 = s^2 - 2r_1(s - r_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"204\" height=\"21\" />, and therefore maximize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/1/341fe6b39ec9ec1977dcb0aa6d25d47242216b33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1(s - r_1) = -r_1^2 + sr_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"179\" height=\"21\" />.  Since this quadratic has a negative leading coefficient, it is maximized at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/5/075f51144d4f56c873506bdb8e4fb7e8ab76d17a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1 = -\\frac{s}{2(-1)} = \\frac{s}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"144\" height=\"39\" />.  In this case, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10ffc19c88f79f96327a6179a75ae03ebb0101ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1 = r_3 = \\frac{s}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"95\" height=\"34\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/c/b9cc171ef6e221019a478b334d06d86a7dce17af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_1 = y_1 + \\frac{s}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"94\" height=\"34\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/8/ce89d15f611a978b010b31e963b636dc039927be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_3 = y_3 + \\frac{s}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"94\" height=\"34\" />.  Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/f/74f334e3c0feab31d78d48a8948383e3f41e5dfd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_3 - z_1 = y_3 - y_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"135\" height=\"16\" />, and the slope of the line is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/3/033ba6c6125fb6b6e918c9b2dc51c31f0051d7fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{z_3 - z_1}{x_3 - x_1} = \\frac{y_3 - y_1}{x_3 - x_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"150\" height=\"40\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, the line of best fit must have slope <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/3/833f4d8068e8772c728948c74739e85b5a0cdbc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(\\textbf{A}) \\frac{y_3 - y_1}{x_3 - x_1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"104\" height=\"51\" />, as any line with a different slope could be improved by replacing it with the line with the same predicted value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/2/0320ab2ddd4939f9072e5316fe8888b0cddee319.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"11\" /> and slope <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e65b99bfefed79dd1c87270b48afddb7fcd9c1c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{y_3 - y_1}{x_3 - x_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"64\" height=\"40\" />.  \n</p><p>-j314andrews\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Apply one of the standard formulae for the gradient of the line of best fit, e.g. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/c/c6ce2b8aff267f8053a9497d9450325ed5566c33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\frac{\\sum {x_i y_i}}{n} - \\bar{x} \\bar{y}}{\\frac{\\sum {x_{i}^2}}{n} - \\bar{x}^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"89\" height=\"55\" />, and substitute in the given condition <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/4/704e55099d6725cf995d28c82cdaef1e1a014a22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_3 - x_2 = x_2 - x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"138\" height=\"10\" />. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/9/d79e0e8ce41b5c08729443bcc258d13ca061ff35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{A}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"24\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Linear_Algebra.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Linear_Algebra)\">Solution 3 (Linear Algebra)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Linear Algebra)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be a matrix and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be vectors. Recall that the least-squares error <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/b/bdbef3f0ca181635a0e1353492ade5d0ffe6f667.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$||Ax - y||^2_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"85\" height=\"21\" /> is minimized when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/d/7ad11ba2af2c1220c6581a31bc500bebb64457ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = (A^T A)^{-1} A^T y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"22\" />.\n</p><p>In this case, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/8/b38f29d445af476c88e192de2898c2f456bbd454.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = \\begin{bmatrix}x_1 &amp;&amp; 1 \\\\ x_2 &amp;&amp; 1 \\\\x_3 &amp;&amp; 1\\end{bmatrix}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -28px\" width=\"124\" height=\"66\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/a/1daaa730977e2b6d027ef363efab889bef3defb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\begin{bmatrix}y_1\\\\y_2\\\\y_3\\end{bmatrix}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -28px\" width=\"76\" height=\"66\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/7544121c90e69f5c4f986338c6c61f0f399280cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\begin{bmatrix}m \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"71\" height=\"45\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are the slope and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-intercept of the line of best fit, respectively.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/2/0c2685354f112460fc6f21ec71e027db081d04a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = x_3 - x_2 = x_2 - x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"176\" height=\"17\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/d/97dc330608028986862dfa68872a3cd3f12a10aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_3 = x_2 + d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/d/bad7c2113d8a36242a2b6fb2b2a1f9e54d6e32a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 = x_2 - d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"17\" />.  Plugging these into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/d/7ad11ba2af2c1220c6581a31bc500bebb64457ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = (A^T A)^{-1} A^T y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"22\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/4/b349f3c4d7e2a3119d721ca5c632b76d8b9f38ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = \\frac{y_3 - y_1}{2d} = \\boxed{(\\textbf{A}) \\frac{y_3 - y_1}{x_3 - x_1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"227\" height=\"51\" />.\n</p><p>-j314andrews\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME\" title=\"1988 AHSME\">1988 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1988 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1988\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 28\">Problem 28</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_30\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Prob